# Activity: Routine Domain Models & SQLite Schema

## 1. Objective & Context
Define the core domain models and database tables for **RF01 — Routine Management (Time Blocks)**. Routines represent structured blocks of the day (e.g., Morning Kickoff, Deep Work, Evening Decompression), enabling time-blocking and real-time execution tracking.

- **Prerequisites:** Feature 01 (Workspace Setup).
- **Target Location:** `crates/core/src/domain/routine/` and `crates/core/migrations/0001_create_routines.sql`.

## 2. Technical Scope & Specifications
- **Database:** SQLite with WAL mode (`PRAGMA journal_mode = WAL`), foreign keys enabled.
- **ORM / Driver:** `sqlx` (`0.8.x` with `sqlite`, `runtime-tokio`, `chrono`, `uuid`).
- **Entity Concepts:**
  - `Routine`: High-level grouping or template (e.g., "Weekday Routine", "Weekend Flow").
  - `TimeBlock`: Scheduled interval within a routine with start time, end time, label, color, and optional category.
  - `RoutineDayLog`: Actual daily execution record storing completion timestamps and adherence state.

## 3. Data Structures & Schema

### Domain Entities (`crates/core/src/domain/routine/models.rs`)
```rust
use chrono::{NaiveTime, Utc, DateTime};
use serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};
use uuid::Uuid;

#[derive(Debug, Clone, Serialize, Deserialize, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub struct Routine {
    pub id: Uuid,
    pub name: String,
    pub description: Option<String>,
    pub is_active: bool,
    pub created_at: DateTime<Utc>,
    pub updated_at: DateTime<Utc>,
}

#[derive(Debug, Clone, Serialize, Deserialize, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub struct TimeBlock {
    pub id: Uuid,
    pub routine_id: Uuid,
    pub name: String,
    pub start_time: NaiveTime, // e.g. 08:00:00
    pub end_time: NaiveTime,   // e.g. 10:30:00
    pub category: String,      // e.g. "Focus", "Health", "Leisure"
    pub color_hex: String,     // e.g. "#4F46E5"
    pub order_index: i32,
}

#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, Serialize, Deserialize, PartialEq, Eq)]
#[serde(rename_all = "lowercase")]
pub enum BlockStatus {
    Pending,
    InProgress,
    Completed,
    Skipped,
}
```

### Database Migration (`migrations/0001_create_routines.sql`)
```sql
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS routines (
    id TEXT PRIMARY KEY NOT NULL,
    name TEXT NOT NULL,
    description TEXT,
    is_active INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 1,
    created_at TEXT NOT NULL,
    updated_at TEXT NOT NULL
);

CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS time_blocks (
    id TEXT PRIMARY KEY NOT NULL,
    routine_id TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES routines(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
    name TEXT NOT NULL,
    start_time TEXT NOT NULL, -- HH:MM:SS format
    end_time TEXT NOT NULL,   -- HH:MM:SS format
    category TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'General',
    color_hex TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT '#6366F1',
    order_index INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,
    created_at TEXT NOT NULL
);

CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_time_blocks_routine_id ON time_blocks(routine_id);
CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_time_blocks_start_time ON time_blocks(start_time);

CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS daily_routine_logs (
    id TEXT PRIMARY KEY NOT NULL,
    time_block_id TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES time_blocks(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
    date TEXT NOT NULL, -- YYYY-MM-DD
    status TEXT NOT NULL CHECK(status IN ('pending', 'in_progress', 'completed', 'skipped')),
    started_at TEXT,
    completed_at TEXT,
    notes TEXT,
    UNIQUE(time_block_id, date)
);

CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_daily_routine_logs_date ON daily_routine_logs(date);
```

## 4. Implementation Steps
1. Add `sqlx = { version = "0.8", features = ["sqlite", "runtime-tokio", "chrono", "uuid", "migrate"] }` to `crates/core/Cargo.toml`.
2. Create migration file `crates/core/migrations/0001_create_routines.sql`.
3. Implement Rust domain structs in `crates/core/src/domain/routine/models.rs`.
4. Derive `sqlx::FromRow` and Serde traits on domain structs.
5. Export module in `crates/core/src/domain/routine/mod.rs`.

## 5. Security, Error Handling & Edge Cases
- **Foreign Key Cascading:** `ON DELETE CASCADE` guarantees removing a Routine deletes all associated TimeBlocks and historical logs without orphan records.
- **Unique Daily Log:** `UNIQUE(time_block_id, date)` prevents duplicate check-in records for the same block on the same calendar day.
- **Time Format Integrity:** Use ISO-8601 string storage (`HH:MM:SS` and `YYYY-MM-DD`) ensuring deterministic sorting in SQLite.

## 6. Verification & Automated Tests
- Test compile-time or migration execution:
  ```rust
  #[tokio::test]
  async fn test_routine_migration_runs() {
      let pool = sqlx::sqlite::SqlitePoolOptions::new()
          .connect("sqlite::memory:")
          .await
          .unwrap();
      sqlx::migrate!("./migrations").run(&pool).await.unwrap();
  }
  ```

## 7. Definition of Done (DoD)
- [ ] Domain structs (`Routine`, `TimeBlock`, `BlockStatus`) defined with Serde and SQLx traits.
- [ ] Migration SQL created with indexes and foreign key constraints.
- [ ] In-memory SQLite migration executes cleanly in test.
